IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1 -- piece dg5, layer 1.
-- Section 228 (consent of stockholders or members in lieu of meeting).
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt of the Delaware Code Online (through 85 Del. Laws, c. 550).
-- It is not the official text. `-- src:N | ...` is line N of that file; an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- Section 114(b)(1) lists section 228 among those that address nonstock corporations by their own terms: subsection (a) is for stockholders of a stock corporation,
-- subsection (b) for members of a nonstock corporation. So the corporation's kind (the core's `Kind of corporation`) is an input to the two sufficiency rules.
-- The date and time of record dates are section 213 (piece dg4); the proxy rules of section 212(c)(2) and (3) are piece dg4; "executed, acknowledged and filed" and the
-- information-processing-system rules of section 116 are piece dg1 -- each is a fact the person can state.
-- Votes are counted in votes, not shares (core; section 212(a)).

§ `Section 228(a) and (b) -- action without a meeting`

-- "signed by the holders of outstanding stock having not less than the minimum number of votes that would be necessary to authorize or take such action
-- at a meeting at which all shares entitled to vote thereon were present and voted": the action's own vote requirement (a Vote requirement of the core)
-- carried against all the votes entitled to be cast on the action (Fork F9).
-- NOTHING: the corporation is not of the kind this subsection speaks to, or the counts cannot be a vote.
-- src:935 | (a) Unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation, any action required by this chapter to be taken at any annual or special meeting of stockholders of a corporation, or any action which may be taken at any annual or special meeting of such stockholders, may be taken without a meeting, without prior notice and without a vote, if a consent or consents, setting forth the action so taken, shall be signed by the holders of outstanding stock having not less than the minimum number of votes that would be necessary to authorize or take such action at a meeting at which all shares entitled to vote thereon were present and voted and shall be delivered to the corporation in the manner required by this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 228(a) (src:935)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vote the action needs at a meeting at which all shares entitled to vote were present and voted` IS A `Vote requirement`
      `the number of votes carried by the consents of the holders of outstanding stock, delivered in the manner the section requires` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes entitled to be cast on the action` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 228(a) the stockholders may take the action without a meeting, without prior notice and without a vote` k `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise` `the vote the action needs at a meeting at which all shares entitled to vote were present and voted` `the number of votes carried by the consents of the holders of outstanding stock, delivered in the manner the section requires` `the number of votes entitled to be cast on the action` MEANS
    IF `the kind is a stock corporation` k
    THEN IF `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE `the vote carries` `the vote the action needs at a meeting at which all shares entitled to vote were present and voted` `the number of votes carried by the consents of the holders of outstanding stock, delivered in the manner the section requires` `the number of votes entitled to be cast on the action`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:936 | (b) Unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation, any action required by this chapter to be taken at a meeting of the members of a nonstock corporation, or any action which may be taken at any meeting of the members of a nonstock corporation, may be taken without a meeting, without prior notice and without a vote, if a consent or consents, setting forth the action so taken, shall be signed by members having not less than the minimum number of votes that would be necessary to authorize or take such action at a meeting at which all members having a right to vote thereon were present and voted and shall be delivered to the corporation in the manner required by this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 228(b) (src:936)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vote the action needs at a meeting at which all members having a right to vote were present and voted` IS A `Vote requirement`
      `the number of votes carried by the consents of the members, delivered in the manner the section requires` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes of the members having a right to vote on the action` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 228(b) the members may take the action without a meeting, without prior notice and without a vote` k `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise` `the vote the action needs at a meeting at which all members having a right to vote were present and voted` `the number of votes carried by the consents of the members, delivered in the manner the section requires` `the number of votes of the members having a right to vote on the action` MEANS
    IF `the kind is a nonstock corporation` k
    THEN IF `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE `the vote carries` `the vote the action needs at a meeting at which all members having a right to vote were present and voted` `the number of votes carried by the consents of the members, delivered in the manner the section requires` `the number of votes of the members having a right to vote on the action`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 228(c) -- the consent: form, timing, who may give it, revocation`

-- out of range: section 213 (piece dg4)
-- out of range: section 116 (piece dg1)
-- out of range: section 212(c)(2) and (3) (piece dg4)
-- src:937 | (c) A consent must be set forth in writing or in an electronic transmission. No consent shall be effective to take the corporate action referred to therein unless consents signed by a sufficient number of holders or members to take action are delivered to the corporation in the manner required by this section within 60 days of the first date on which a consent is so delivered to the corporation. Any person executing a consent may provide, whether through instruction to an agent or otherwise, that such consent will be effective at a future time, including a time determined upon the happening of an event, occurring not later than 60 days after such instruction is given or such provision is made, if evidence of the instruction or provision is provided to the corporation. If the person is not a stockholder or member of record when the consent is executed, the consent shall not be valid unless the person is a stockholder or member of record as of the record date for determining stockholders or members entitled to consent to the action. Unless otherwise provided, any such consent shall be revocable prior to its becoming effective. All references to a “consent” in this section means a consent permitted by this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 228(c) (src:937)
DECLARE `dg5 s 228 Consent delivered to the corporation` HAS
    `the consent is set forth in writing or in an electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the way the consent was delivered`                                      IS A `dg5 s 228(d)(1) Way a consent is delivered`
    `the consent was delivered by hand or by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consent was reproduced and delivered in paper form`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the corporation has designated the information processing system`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consent sets forth or is delivered with information that enables the corporation to determine the date of delivery and the identity of the person giving it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consent is given by a person authorized to act for a stockholder or member as proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that proxy's consent complies with s 212(c)(2) and (3)`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date on which the consent was delivered to the corporation`         IS A DATE
    `the consent is to be effective at a future time`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date on which the instruction or provision for the future time was given` IS A DATE
    `the date of the future time at which the consent is to be effective`    IS A DATE
    `evidence of the instruction or provision for the future time was provided to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the signer was a stockholder or member of record when the consent was executed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the signer was a stockholder or member of record on the record date for determining those entitled to consent to the action` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consent was revoked before it became effective`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consent is made irrevocable by a provision otherwise providing`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of votes the consent carries`                               IS A NUMBER

-- src:938 | (d) (1) A consent permitted by this section shall be delivered: (i) to the principal place of business of the corporation; (ii) to an officer or agent of the corporation having custody of the book in which proceedings of meetings of stockholders or members are recorded; (iii) to the registered office of the corporation in this State by hand or by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested; or (iv) subject to the next sentence, in accordance with § 116 of this title to an information processing system, if any, designated by the corporation for receiving such consents. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 228(d)(1) (src:938)
DECLARE `dg5 s 228(d)(1) Way a consent is delivered` IS ONE OF
    `to the principal place of business of the corporation`
    `to an officer or agent of the corporation having custody of the book in which proceedings of meetings of stockholders or members are recorded`
    `to the registered office of the corporation in this State`
    `to an information processing system designated by the corporation for receiving consents, in accordance with section 116`

-- src:937 | A consent must be set forth in writing or in an electronic transmission. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 228(c) (src:937)
GIVEN c IS A `dg5 s 228 Consent delivered to the corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 228(c) the consent is set forth in a permitted form` c MEANS
    c's `the consent is set forth in writing or in an electronic transmission`

-- Delivery: (i) the principal place of business; (ii) an officer or agent having custody of the book of proceedings; (iii) the registered office by hand or by certified or
-- registered mail, return receipt requested; or (iv) an information processing system designated by the corporation, in accordance with section 116, with information that
-- enables the corporation to determine the date of delivery and the identity of the person giving the consent, and, if given by a proxy, in compliance with section 212(c)(2) and (3).
-- Paragraph (d)(2): "if such consent is delivered pursuant to clause (i), (ii) or (iii) ... such consent must be reproduced and delivered in paper form."
-- src:938 | (d) (1) A consent permitted by this section shall be delivered: (i) to the principal place of business of the corporation; (ii) to an officer or agent of the corporation having custody of the book in which proceedings of meetings of stockholders or members are recorded; (iii) to the registered office of the corporation in this State by hand or by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested; or (iv) subject to the next sentence, in accordance with § 116 of this title to an information processing system, if any, designated by the corporation for receiving such consents. In the case of delivery pursuant to the foregoing clause (iv), such consent must set forth or be delivered with information that enables the corporation to determine the date of delivery of such consent and the identity of the person giving such consent, and, if such consent is given by a person authorized to act for a stockholder or member as proxy, such consent must comply with the applicable provisions of § 212(c)(2) and (3) of this title.
-- src:939 | provided that if such consent is delivered pursuant to clause (i), (ii) or (iii) of paragraph (d)(1) of this section, such consent must be reproduced and delivered in paper form.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 228(d)(1) (src:938); § 228(d)(2) (src:939)
GIVEN c IS A `dg5 s 228 Consent delivered to the corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 228(d)(1) the consent was delivered in a permitted way` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the way the consent was delivered`
    WHEN `to the principal place of business of the corporation` THEN
        c's `the consent was reproduced and delivered in paper form`
    WHEN `to an officer or agent of the corporation having custody of the book in which proceedings of meetings of stockholders or members are recorded` THEN
        c's `the consent was reproduced and delivered in paper form`
    WHEN `to the registered office of the corporation in this State` THEN
            c's `the consent was delivered by hand or by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested`
        AND c's `the consent was reproduced and delivered in paper form`
    WHEN `to an information processing system designated by the corporation for receiving consents, in accordance with section 116` THEN
            c's `the corporation has designated the information processing system`
        AND c's `the consent sets forth or is delivered with information that enables the corporation to determine the date of delivery and the identity of the person giving it`
        AND ((NOT c's `the consent is given by a person authorized to act for a stockholder or member as proxy`) OR c's `that proxy's consent complies with s 212(c)(2) and (3)`)

-- "All references to a 'consent' in this section means a consent permitted by this section": a consent in a permitted form, delivered in a permitted way.
-- src:937 | All references to a “consent” in this section means a consent permitted by this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 228(c) (src:937)
GIVEN c IS A `dg5 s 228 Consent delivered to the corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 228(c) the consent is a consent permitted by this section` c MEANS
        `s 228(c) the consent is set forth in a permitted form` c
    AND `s 228(d)(1) the consent was delivered in a permitted way` c

-- "within 60 days of the first date on which a consent is so delivered": the last day, the first date plus 60 days, is inside (Fork F3).
-- src:937 | No consent shall be effective to take the corporate action referred to therein unless consents signed by a sufficient number of holders or members to take action are delivered to the corporation in the manner required by this section within 60 days of the first date on which a consent is so delivered to the corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 228(c) (src:937)
GIVEN `the first date on which a consent was delivered to the corporation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 228(c) the last day for sufficient consents to be delivered` `the first date on which a consent was delivered to the corporation` MEANS
    `the date` (`period in days` 60) `after` `the first date on which a consent was delivered to the corporation`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 228(c) (src:937)
GIVEN c IS A `dg5 s 228 Consent delivered to the corporation`
      `the first date on which a consent was delivered to the corporation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 228(c) the consent was delivered within 60 days of the first date on which a consent was delivered` c `the first date on which a consent was delivered to the corporation` MEANS
    c's `the date on which the consent was delivered to the corporation` AT MOST (`s 228(c) the last day for sufficient consents to be delivered` `the first date on which a consent was delivered to the corporation`)

-- "effective at a future time, including a time determined upon the happening of an event, occurring not later than 60 days after such instruction is given or such provision is made,
-- if evidence of the instruction or provision is provided to the corporation."
-- src:937 | Any person executing a consent may provide, whether through instruction to an agent or otherwise, that such consent will be effective at a future time, including a time determined upon the happening of an event, occurring not later than 60 days after such instruction is given or such provision is made, if evidence of the instruction or provision is provided to the corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 228(c) (src:937)
GIVEN c IS A `dg5 s 228 Consent delivered to the corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 228(c) the future effectiveness of the consent is permitted` c MEANS
        (NOT c's `the consent is to be effective at a future time`)
     OR (    c's `evidence of the instruction or provision for the future time was provided to the corporation`
         AND c's `the date of the future time at which the consent is to be effective`
               AT MOST (`the date` (`period in days` 60) `after` (c's `the date on which the instruction or provision for the future time was given`)))

-- "If the person is not a stockholder or member of record when the consent is executed, the consent shall not be valid unless the person is a stockholder or member of record
-- as of the record date for determining stockholders or members entitled to consent to the action."
-- src:937 | If the person is not a stockholder or member of record when the consent is executed, the consent shall not be valid unless the person is a stockholder or member of record as of the record date for determining stockholders or members entitled to consent to the action. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 228(c) (src:937)
GIVEN c IS A `dg5 s 228 Consent delivered to the corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 228(c) the signer was a holder of record in time` c MEANS
        c's `the signer was a stockholder or member of record when the consent was executed`
     OR c's `the signer was a stockholder or member of record on the record date for determining those entitled to consent to the action`

-- "Unless otherwise provided, any such consent shall be revocable prior to its becoming effective."
-- src:937 | Unless otherwise provided, any such consent shall be revocable prior to its becoming effective. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 228(c) (src:937)
GIVEN c IS A `dg5 s 228 Consent delivered to the corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 228(c) the consent was effectively revoked` c MEANS
        c's `the consent was revoked before it became effective`
    AND (NOT c's `the consent is made irrevocable by a provision otherwise providing`)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 228(c) (src:937)
GIVEN c IS A `dg5 s 228 Consent delivered to the corporation`
      `the first date on which a consent was delivered to the corporation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 228(c) the consent counts toward the action` c `the first date on which a consent was delivered to the corporation` MEANS
        `s 228(c) the consent is a consent permitted by this section` c
    AND `s 228(c) the consent was delivered within 60 days of the first date on which a consent was delivered` c `the first date on which a consent was delivered to the corporation`
    AND `s 228(c) the future effectiveness of the consent is permitted` c
    AND `s 228(c) the signer was a holder of record in time` c
    AND (NOT (`s 228(c) the consent was effectively revoked` c))

-- The votes of the consents that count: the figure that subsections (a) and (b) compare with the vote the action needs.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 228(a) (src:935); § 228(b) (src:936); § 228(c) (src:937)
GIVEN cs IS A LIST OF `dg5 s 228 Consent delivered to the corporation`
      `the first date on which a consent was delivered to the corporation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 228(c) the votes carried by the consents that count` cs `the first date on which a consent was delivered to the corporation` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN c YIELD IF `s 228(c) the consent counts toward the action` c `the first date on which a consent was delivered to the corporation` THEN c's `the number of votes the consent carries` ELSE 0) cs)

§ `Section 228(d)(2) -- copies and electronic signatures`

-- src:939 | Any copy, facsimile or other reliable reproduction of a consent in writing may be substituted or used in lieu of the original writing for any and all purposes for which the original writing could be used, provided that such copy, facsimile or other reproduction shall be a complete reproduction of the entire original writing. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 228(d)(2) (src:939)
GIVEN `the copy, facsimile or other reproduction is a complete reproduction of the entire original writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 228(d)(2) the reproduction may be used in lieu of the original writing` `the copy, facsimile or other reproduction is a complete reproduction of the entire original writing` MEANS
    `the copy, facsimile or other reproduction is a complete reproduction of the entire original writing`

-- out of range: section 116 (piece dg1)
-- src:939 | A consent may be documented and signed in accordance with § 116 of this title, and when so documented or signed shall be deemed to be in writing for purposes of this title; provided that if such consent is delivered pursuant to clause (i), (ii) or (iii) of paragraph (d)(1) of this section, such consent must be reproduced and delivered in paper form.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 228(d)(2) (src:939)
GIVEN `the consent is documented and signed in accordance with s 116` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 228(d)(2) the consent is deemed to be in writing` `the consent is documented and signed in accordance with s 116` MEANS
    `the consent is documented and signed in accordance with s 116`

§ `Section 228(e) -- notice of action by less than unanimous consent`

-- out of range: section 213 (piece dg4)
-- "prompt notice of the taking of the action by consent shall be given to those stockholders or members as of the record date for the action by consent who have not consented
-- and who would have been entitled to notice of the meeting if the action had been taken at a meeting and the record date for the notice of the meeting were the record date for the action by consent."
-- src:940 | If an action by consent under subsections (a) or (b) of this section has been taken by stockholders or members by less than unanimous consent, prompt notice of the taking of the action by consent shall be given to those stockholders or members as of the record date for the action by consent who have not consented and who would have been entitled to notice of the meeting if the action had been taken at a meeting and the record date for the notice of the meeting were the record date for the action by consent. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 228(e) (src:940)
GIVEN `the action was taken by less than unanimous consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was a stockholder or member on the record date for the action by consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person would have been entitled to notice of the meeting if the action had been taken at a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 228(e) prompt notice of the taking of the action must be given to the person` `the action was taken by less than unanimous consent` `the person was a stockholder or member on the record date for the action by consent` `the person has consented` `the person would have been entitled to notice of the meeting if the action had been taken at a meeting` MEANS
        `the action was taken by less than unanimous consent`
    AND `the person was a stockholder or member on the record date for the action by consent`
    AND (NOT `the person has consented`)
    AND `the person would have been entitled to notice of the meeting if the action had been taken at a meeting`

-- out of range: the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (federal law, not among the inputs)
-- src:940 | The notice required by this subsection may be provided by a notice which constitutes a notice of internet availability of proxy materials under rules promulgated under the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, 15 U.S.C. § 78a et seq. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 228(e) (src:940)
GIVEN `the notice constitutes a notice of internet availability of proxy materials under rules promulgated under the Securities Exchange Act of 1934` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 228(e) the notice may be provided by a notice of internet availability of proxy materials` `the notice constitutes a notice of internet availability of proxy materials under rules promulgated under the Securities Exchange Act of 1934` MEANS
    `the notice constitutes a notice of internet availability of proxy materials under rules promulgated under the Securities Exchange Act of 1934`

-- The certificate filed under another section "shall state, in lieu of any statement required by such section concerning any vote of stockholders or members, that consent has been given in accordance with this section".
-- src:940 | In the event that the action which is consented to is such as would have required the filing of a certificate under any other section of this title, if such action had been voted on by stockholders or by members at a meeting thereof, the certificate filed under such other section shall state, in lieu of any statement required by such section concerning any vote of stockholders or members, that consent has been given in accordance with this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 228(e) (src:940)
GIVEN `the action consented to would have required the filing of a certificate under another section of this title if it had been voted on at a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 228(e) the certificate must state that consent has been given in accordance with section 228 in lieu of the statement about a vote` `the action consented to would have required the filing of a certificate under another section of this title if it had been voted on at a meeting` MEANS
    `the action consented to would have required the filing of a certificate under another section of this title if it had been voted on at a meeting`
